==History==
===1851–1896===
{{Main|History of The New York Times (1851–1896)|label1 = History of ''The New York Times'' (1851–1896)}}

{{multiple image
|total_width=500

| image1= 18510831 prospectus of "New-York Daily Times" (The New York Times).png |caption1= This pre-publication prospectus presented the newspaper's philosophies, including that it "will canvass freely the character and pretensions of Public Men, the merits and demerits of all administrations of Government, National, State and Municipal, and the worth of all institutions, principles, habits and professions".<ref name="NYTimes_20260104">{{cite news |last1=Dunlap |first1=David W. |date=January 4, 2026 |title=The Birth of The Times / A prospectus in 1851 announced the arrival of a daily newspaper you might be familiar with. |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/01/04/insider/the-birth-of-the-times.html |newspaper=The New York Times}} ([https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/01/04/pageoneplus/04a3_intimespast/04a3_intimespast-superJumbo.jpg?quality=75&auto=webp direct link to image] and [https://web.archive.org/web/20260214154442/https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/01/04/pageoneplus/04a3_intimespast/04a3_intimespast-superJumbo.jpg?quality=75&auto=webp archive thereof])</ref>

| image2= First NYTimes frontpage (1851-9-18).png |caption2= The first issue of ''The New York Times''—initially called the ''New-York Daily Times''—was published on Thursday, September 18, 1851. The name was changed in 1857 to ''The New-York Times'' after the evening edition was suspended, and the hyphen was dropped in 1896.<ref name=NYTimes_20260104/>
